WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:20.367
Izzie knew the campers were doing something messy today.

2
00:00:20.368 --> 00:00:23.885
The picnic table was covered with garbage bags.

3
00:00:23.886 --> 00:00:27.838
And Mr. Dunn was wearing an apron and rubber gloves.

4
00:00:27.839 --> 00:00:30.305
"Great!" Izzie thought.

5
00:00:30.306 --> 00:00:33.279
Messy meant fun!

6
00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:37.036
"It looks like Laundry Day," Bobby said.

7
00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:40.995
He pointed to a bucket of water filled with T-shirts.

8
00:00:40.996 --> 00:00:44.359
"Nope," Mr. Dunn said with a smile.

9
00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:48.286
"It's Tie-dyed T-shirt Day!"

10
00:00:48.287 --> 00:00:51.992
Mr. Dunn held up a blue and green T-shirt.

11
00:00:51.993 --> 00:00:57.909
It was tie-dyed and had the words "Kids Central Summer Camp" on it.

12
00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:02.737
"Awesome!" Izzie cried. "I want that shirt!

13
00:01:02.738 --> 00:01:06.291
I'm going to make one exactly like it."

14
00:01:06.292 --> 00:01:11.360
"Grab your aprons and a pair of gloves, campers," said Mr. Dunn.

15
00:01:11.361 --> 00:01:15.378
"You don't want the dye getting on your skin or clothes.

16
00:01:15.379 --> 00:01:20.649
Only on the shirt you're dying!" Mr. Dunn chuckled.

17
00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:24.633
"Start by choosing a T-shirt from the bucket."

18
00:01:24.634 --> 00:01:30.126
Mr. Dunn showed the campers how to wring the water out of the shirts.

19
00:01:30.127 --> 00:01:35.175
"Now we're ready to make our designs," he said.

20
00:01:35.176 --> 00:01:38.045
"Can anyone guess how I made mine?"

21
00:01:38.046 --> 00:01:41.967
Izzie studied his shirt.

22
00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:46.895
She also saw rubber bands on the table.

23
00:01:46.896 --> 00:01:51.983
"You put rubber bands around the T-shirt before you dyed it!" Izzie said.

24
00:01:51.984 --> 00:01:54.533
"The dye couldn't get under the rubber bands.

25
00:01:54.534 --> 00:01:57.729
That's why there are those white stripes!"

26
00:01:57.730 --> 00:02:02.225
Mr. Dunn smiled. "Good thinking, Izzie."

27
00:02:02.226 --> 00:02:06.471
"First twist your shirt," the teacher said.

28
00:02:06.472 --> 00:02:10.339
"Then make sections with rubber bands.

29
00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:15.520
Each rubber band will become a white stripe.

30
00:02:15.521 --> 00:02:20.634
To make a pattern of circles, twist the middle section of the shirt.

31
00:02:20.635 --> 00:02:25.069
Add rubber bands to make rings around your circle."

32
00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:29.634
"I want stripes, just like yours, Mr. Dunn," Izzie said.

33
00:02:29.635 --> 00:02:33.088
"I'm making circles," said Nina.

34
00:02:33.089 --> 00:02:39.871
The boys chose circles too.

35
00:02:39.872 --> 00:02:42.692
"Now it's time to dye.

36
00:02:42.693 --> 00:02:46.173
Carefully squeeze dye onto each section."

37
00:02:46.174 --> 00:02:51.709
Mr. Dunn demonstrated.

38
00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:57.697
"You can use just two colors, or as many as you want," Mr. Dunn said.

39
00:02:57.698 --> 00:03:00.488
Izzie looked at Mr. Dunn's shirt.

40
00:03:00.489 --> 00:03:04.791
It had green stripes at the top and blue ones at the bottom.

41
00:03:04.792 --> 00:03:08.213
Izzie used those colors too.

42
00:03:08.214 --> 00:03:11.561
"Now put the shirts in plastic bags.

43
00:03:11.562 --> 00:03:17.105
The dye needs to soak in for the rest of the day," said Mr. Dunn.

44
00:03:17.106 --> 00:03:22.058
"At home you'll have to hang up the shirts to let them dry."

45
00:03:22.059 --> 00:03:25.281
The kids set their bagged shirts aside.

46
00:03:25.282 --> 00:03:27.841
But Izzie wasn't good at waiting.

47
00:03:27.842 --> 00:03:30.962
She wanted to see her shirt now.

48
00:03:30.963 --> 00:03:35.367
"Can we peek at the shirts, to check our designs?" she asked.

49
00:03:35.368 --> 00:03:38.695
"No." Mr. Dunn shook his head.

50
00:03:38.696 --> 00:03:44.999
"You have to wait, Izzie."

51
00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:48.701
"Waiting is so hard," Izzie thought.

52
00:03:48.702 --> 00:03:51.419
What if she had made a mistake?

53
00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:55.039
What if her shirt didn't come out like Mr. Dunn's?

54
00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:58.959
Finally the teacher announced, "It's time!"

55
00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:05.341
The kids rushed back to their shirts.

56
00:04:05.342 --> 00:04:08.871
Izzie thought the other campers' shirts looked great.

57
00:04:08.872 --> 00:04:13.863
Then she took hers out of the bag.

58
00:04:13.864 --> 00:04:20.133
She gasped. There were only two green stripes and five blue ones.

59
00:04:20.134 --> 00:04:28.820
"Mr. Dunn, it doesn't look like your shirt at all!" she cried.

60
00:04:28.821 --> 00:04:33.146
"It's much better than my shirt," Mr. Dunn said.

61
00:04:33.147 --> 00:04:36.689
"The uneven pattern is beautiful!

62
00:04:36.690 --> 00:04:41.499
You'll see how great it looks when we all wear our shirts on Friday."

63
00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:51.727
Izzie smiled. Now she couldn't wait until Friday!
